# OpenClaw Environment Setup & Dance HF Demo

Step-by-step guide to set up the Mini Pupper with OpenClaw and run the Hugging Face dance demo.

---

## 1. Flash the SD Card

Flash a fresh Raspberry Pi OS (Ubuntu) image onto the SD card using your preferred tool (Raspberry Pi Imager, `dd`, etc.).

---

## 2. Clone Repositories

On the Pi (user `ubuntu`): //will need to change the github repo https

```bash
# Main app
git clone https://github.com/gracereginalayndra/Minipupper-Openclaw-Backup-2.git ~/minipupper-app

# Robot control stack
git clone https://github.com/gracereginalayndra/Minipupper-Openclaw-Backup-2.git ~/StanfordQuadruped/
```

---

## 3. Service Account Credentials

Place the Google Cloud service account JSON key on the Pi:

```bash
nano ~/apps-md-robots/20250923.json
```

Paste the contents of your `20250923.json` key file, then save.

---

## 4. Install Node.js

```bash
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_22.x | sudo -E bash -
sudo apt install -y nodejs

# Configure global npm prefix (avoids sudo for global installs)
mkdir -p ~/.npm-global
npm config set prefix '~/.npm-global'
echo 'export PATH=~/.npm-global/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
```

---

## 5. Install OpenClaw

```bash
npm install -g openclaw@2026.5.7

# Verify
openclaw --version
```

